#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124574 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124382 :question/id #uuid "09d12c46-4ac8-53d9-80a6-ca68f98e0c5a" :question/math-academy-id "e-7184" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)  = \\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = yz\\,\\mathbf{i} + (xz + 4z^2)\\,\\mathbf{j} + (xy+8yz)\\,\\mathbf{k}.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z) = \\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{x}} \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{y}} \\, \\mathbf{j} + \\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{z}} \\, \\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)  = \\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{x}} = yz, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{y}} = xz + 4z^2, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{z}} = xy+8yz.\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{x}}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int yz\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =xyz+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{y}} = xz + \\dfrac{\\partial{g}}{\\partial{y}}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{y}} = xz + 4z^2$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xz+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =xz+4{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =4{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\dfrac{\\partial{g}}{\\partial{y}}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 4{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4y{z}^{2}+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z) = 4yz^2 + h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x, y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z) = xyz + 4yz^2 + h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{z}} = xy + 8yz + h'(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\dfrac{\\partial{f}}{\\partial{z}} = xy+8yz$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy+8yz & =xy+8yz+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z) = xyz + 4yz^2 + C.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90458c6e-3d72-5235-a1c0-627fe4fd2855" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186730341 :question-generator/id #uuid "5d4b524b-21d9-50b8-9287-8242fa93e46b" :question-generator/script "generators/b3/b38250818a439d2949e076361386629ab4166913fe4069cbc77c1c15a411c088/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125024 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8219c68e-f3f4-56a9-8dee-80eaf456059c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x, y, z) = x^{2}y + 2yz + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122745} {:answer/id #uuid "9ee2dd6e-a063-5ce6-ba25-1e01e48c63c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x, y, z) = x^{2}y - 3yz + Cz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122746} {:answer/id #uuid "c8899973-d846-566d-aff8-1ee753154df7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x, y, z) = xy^{2} + 2yz + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122747} {:answer/id #uuid "2d271ef1-cc52-51d9-8679-408b178e46be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x, y, z) = x^{2}yz + yz^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122748} {:answer/id #uuid "5833e6fd-e2cb-5015-9115-e437b9926197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x, y, z) = x^{2}y + yz + Cxz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8219c68e-f3f4-56a9-8dee-80eaf456059c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x, y, z) = x^{2}y + 2yz + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122745} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2a39a8c-dc65-5667-9694-693d1c689df2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122744}] :question/id #uuid "b00bfeb0-ca4e-5b6e-8b0c-afb0a62e4170" :question/math-academy-id "q-36977" :question/problem "Find $f(x, y, z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)$, where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=2xy\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+({x}^{2}+2z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+2y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}$." :question/worked-solution "Integrate $f_x=2xy$ with respect to $x$: $f=x^2y+g(y,z)$. Matching $f_y=x^2+2z$ gives $g_y=2z$, so $g=2yz+h(z)$. Finally $f_z=2y+h'(z)=2y$, hence $h$ is constant. Therefore $$f=x^2y+2yz+C.$$ Its three partial derivatives reproduce all components of $F$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03292879-7e19-58c5-bf30-9a82b7757e44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406660} {:answer/id #uuid "10ef096b-3da6-5469-9aaf-056abb9c9b31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406663} {:answer/id #uuid "2e5e2bd6-42c5-529f-9f08-cbd53403ea48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406668} {:answer/id #uuid "b1384745-a3d2-57a2-83cf-2248f12bae46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406683} {:answer/id #uuid "c18a0f77-fbcd-5ceb-b30c-ca0b3feee4c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+z\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03292879-7e19-58c5-bf30-9a82b7757e44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406660} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7b902c9-1d56-5de9-9587-969c0111a4bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406695}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7faa34ab-beed-5e97-be56-8c5b15402d1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-81739" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=(\\operatorname{cos}z+y\\operatorname{cos}x)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{sin}x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}-x\\operatorname{sin}z\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,k.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z & =-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259726 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01ec042b-d1ae-56d2-9c3b-5e465e3d4cd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{z}^{2}+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256801} {:answer/id #uuid "1ceac5b9-64e6-5124-a6a6-85b5d1310188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257021} {:answer/id #uuid "5bd04f96-05c9-5672-a88f-0279e73ffdd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy+{x}^{2}z+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257581} {:answer/id #uuid "f7f96662-a242-51e6-8a22-278c74c24b3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}-z\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258957} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc740e7-8445-5753-9183-33d9b76eb7e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+yz+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ceac5b9-64e6-5124-a6a6-85b5d1310188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257021} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3c753f6-334f-50c7-9748-b981b710da38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259320}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "16cbb2e0-e24c-5276-8cc2-e4e9a9ed6115" :question/math-academy-id "q-124729" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=(2xz+\\operatorname{sin}y)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+x\\operatorname{cos}y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+{x}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2xz+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2xz+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}z+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={x}^{2}+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={x}^{2}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259727 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1602f189-0d28-56ae-9dd9-e128132e6ed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}+yz-{e}^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256980} {:answer/id #uuid "56a824e1-89ad-5b9f-9d90-0a15c3c6afec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xyz-y{e}^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257529} {:answer/id #uuid "83844a24-d36a-5bde-90cc-25704c4bd024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257944} {:answer/id #uuid "9676b23d-58f9-5906-86c8-bc56f352ddbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{3}{y}^{2}+xz-{e}^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258109} {:answer/id #uuid "fbfef173-d55d-5471-9bd3-2a9896819991" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={y}^{3}z-x{e}^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83844a24-d36a-5bde-90cc-25704c4bd024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257944} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf730883-1f0b-511a-85de-b890c410b87c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259364}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "af3748dd-98e9-5ccb-8f93-b1501896f383" :question/math-academy-id "q-124733" :question/problem "Consider the function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=({y}^{2}{z}^{3}-{e}^{z})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2xy{z}^{3}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+(3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{\\text{i}}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{\\text{j}}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{\\text{k}}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={y}^{2}{z}^{3}-{e}^{z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2xy{z}^{3},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({y}^{2}{z}^{3}-{e}^{z})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2xy{z}^{3}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2xy{z}^{3}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2xy{z}^{3}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =2xy{z}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}+{h}^{′}(z) & =3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z} \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266132 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61fd2894-92e2-5f21-a8ef-3e4ce0f75c87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xz\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+{x}^{2}-y{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263843} {:answer/id #uuid "79e27da1-668f-5a0d-929e-edada25fd557" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+xy-y{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264058} {:answer/id #uuid "7c4936ba-0c0b-5085-a53f-9463a50276eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+xy+x{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264073} {:answer/id #uuid "ab37d3c3-0675-5158-a1cc-82765ce5104b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+x-y{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264470} {:answer/id #uuid "f52f7f29-86a2-537c-90f4-0eabb7389f49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+xz-{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab37d3c3-0675-5158-a1cc-82765ce5104b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+x-y{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264470} :answer-field/id #uuid "a355c26c-a760-5643-9305-ddb34ec96b30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265532}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "062ec003-5729-5fe0-9819-864cef26e212" :question/math-academy-id "q-132100" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=(\\operatorname{ln}y+1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(\\frac{x}{y}-{z}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}-2yz\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{y}-{z}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-2yz\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+x+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{y}-{z}^{2}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{x}{y}-{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =-{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int (-{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-y{z}^{2}+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=-y{z}^{2}+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+x-y{z}^{2}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-2yz+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-2yz$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2yz & =-2yz+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+x-y{z}^{2}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266133 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "005532ea-a569-5e6b-9518-a0150b3fb329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xyz{e}^{z}+x+y-{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263006} {:answer/id #uuid "7d7694c1-e825-574d-a180-e04f18376fc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy{e}^{z}+{x}^{2}+x+{y}^{2}z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264082} {:answer/id #uuid "a49fbc3b-b203-5f1b-8f40-b0bcdbe9fbb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{z}+y{x}^{2}+x-{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264402} {:answer/id #uuid "c04be1f6-81c5-54c2-ba54-5b752c684e10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy{e}^{z}+x+y-z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264673} {:answer/id #uuid "c6d7254b-5172-5dfd-9ea1-9404e617cc8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy{e}^{z}+{x}^{2}+y-{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6d7254b-5172-5dfd-9ea1-9404e617cc8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy{e}^{z}+{x}^{2}+y-{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264739} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9c4e81f-33ab-54ad-9dac-693d04696388" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265624}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6b7d90b3-0384-5231-a89f-b7683283ef28" :question/math-academy-id "q-132103" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=(2x+y{e}^{z})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(x{e}^{z}+1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+(xy{e}^{z}-2z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x+y{e}^{z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{z}+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{z}-2z\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2x+y{e}^{z})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+xy{e}^{z}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{z}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{z}+1$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{z}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =x{e}^{z}+1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int \\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =y+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=y+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+xy{e}^{z}+y+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{z}+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{z}-2z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy{e}^{z}-2z & =xy{e}^{z}+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =-2z \\\\ h(z) & =-{z}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=xy{e}^{z}+{x}^{2}+y-{z}^{2}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323869 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25284915-404f-5375-ac86-a55e513a4466" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2yz+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321435} {:answer/id #uuid "30d3adbe-dcd7-5a7c-b7f4-9d8234912198" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+y{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321523} {:answer/id #uuid "4ae0e8e2-a744-52a6-8ad3-e46566c11f8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+{y}^{2}z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321736} {:answer/id #uuid "acc3c980-cbdd-5610-8d47-878be5ead5e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+yz+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322501} {:answer/id #uuid "b7050df8-a7aa-52e2-bfb8-36dddf3c124d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+2{y}^{2}z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ae0e8e2-a744-52a6-8ad3-e46566c11f8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+{y}^{2}z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321736} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0c9f1ab-635a-52c8-a0fd-14bac3805bc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323548}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f96b761e-8386-56f5-990d-c8300f6fbe05" :question/math-academy-id "q-36978" :question/problem "Consider the function\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,i+2yz\\,j+{y}^{2}\\,k.\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{\\text{i}}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{\\text{j}}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{\\text{k}}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2yz,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={y}^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2yz$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =2yz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int (2yz)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={y}^{2}z+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)={y}^{2}z+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+{y}^{2}z+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={y}^{2}+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={y}^{2}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+{h}^{′}(z) & ={y}^{2} \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+{y}^{2}z+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351358 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16fb8477-c52e-58fb-b8cf-7472dfb09f3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy+yz+xz+y+z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348639} {:answer/id #uuid "1a6aa838-2967-5f6d-9ea6-bf9875d95e2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xyz+xz+xy+yz+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348670} {:answer/id #uuid "955bbc49-7db4-56b7-a02a-3e024df98843" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy+yz+x+y+z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349787} {:answer/id #uuid "9e6dc831-45cc-555d-ac7f-a066307d2999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xyz+x+y+z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349861} {:answer/id #uuid "d71375c9-4e61-53ba-b6da-07758eef80e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy+yz+xz+x+y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "955bbc49-7db4-56b7-a02a-3e024df98843" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy+yz+x+y+z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349787} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb7814d3-6540-596e-89a1-188d1c44755f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351031}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e18f3bc6-6740-5752-becc-b988af5a59c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-81740" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where $F(x,y,z)=(y+1)\\,i+(x+z+1)\\,j+(y+1)\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x+z+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=y+1\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (y+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =xy+x+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x+z+1$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =x+z+1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =z+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int (z+1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =yz+y+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=yz+y+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=xy+x+yz+y+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=y+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=y+1$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+1 & =y+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =1 \\\\ h(z) & =z+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=xy+yz+x+y+z+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351359 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cca9c71-9e8d-570c-8946-ced4f1d50328" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348697} {:answer/id #uuid "2a68e94a-4173-5ae7-858e-76a0731e97f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348821} {:answer/id #uuid "58860516-bdb9-5c40-81cc-99fbd0564951" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=(x+y){e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349259} {:answer/id #uuid "5cca20bd-b007-5611-a5cf-cd625413e2d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{xy}+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349300} {:answer/id #uuid "d106b7ad-431a-5269-9f98-9101b7fb0c7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xy}+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a68e94a-4173-5ae7-858e-76a0731e97f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348821} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7a6d5b1-1736-5e32-bd6e-3958724c6738" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351115}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e91b9e21-1500-52f9-9378-332978dc9aa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-81741" :question/problem "Consider the function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xy}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+x{e}^{xy}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+3\\operatorname{cos}(3z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{\\text{i}}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{\\text{j}}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{\\text{k}}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y{e}^{xy},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{xy}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =x{e}^{xy} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(z) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z) \\\\ h(z) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351364 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2805a157-0ff6-5513-9530-54816d9d026a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy{z}^{2}+yz-2z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348790} {:answer/id #uuid "55830456-e7d8-5981-846c-7a4fe6003b50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2xyz+y-2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349229} {:answer/id #uuid "6146406d-3af2-5ae5-90e5-08d79844f945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xyz+yz-z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349337} {:answer/id #uuid "a1b8df1f-1d2d-5411-8b30-3ebb1730a80f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2xyz+yz-2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349887} {:answer/id #uuid "b0f652e8-b915-5303-b15e-d17266e3544c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2xy{z}^{2}+y-z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2805a157-0ff6-5513-9530-54816d9d026a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy{z}^{2}+yz-2z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348790} :answer-field/id #uuid "35fcc368-86fe-5787-a4dc-f3208dbfc229" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350800}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "98c97ef5-5ea8-5162-8c84-a1645b2982e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-81751" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=y{z}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(x{z}^{2}+z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+(2xyz+y-2)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y{z}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{z}^{2}+z,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=2xyz+y-2\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int y{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =xy{z}^{2}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{z}^{2}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{z}^{2}+z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{z}^{2}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =x{z}^{2}+z \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =yz+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=yz+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=xy{z}^{2}+yz+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=2xyz+y+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=2xyz+y-2$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2xyz+y-2 & =2xyz+y+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =-2 \\\\ h(z) & =-2z+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=xy{z}^{2}+yz-2z+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351365 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16c1bf68-0a65-5287-b32f-c0e4dc3478f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xz{e}^{xz}+xz+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348638} {:answer/id #uuid "bd1acbc8-d106-5b62-8d36-a7cb3a78a863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xz}+yz+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350128} {:answer/id #uuid "d83bed69-94c4-50e6-be9a-7dcda2208ee0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xz{e}^{xz}+y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350341} {:answer/id #uuid "f516143d-39f1-5b86-9e6a-3fe23efc5edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xz}+xy+z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350590} {:answer/id #uuid "fda21360-2a77-5e5c-bdf6-2c33643d2238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xz}+xz+y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fda21360-2a77-5e5c-bdf6-2c33643d2238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xz}+xz+y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350678} :answer-field/id #uuid "b222692b-cb3d-5740-9bf6-1564da255bac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351013}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dfdbf33d-2f2f-5cc3-b43d-2537f87d3a7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-81752" :question/problem "Consider the function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=(yz{e}^{xz}+z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+({e}^{xz}+1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+(xy{e}^{xz}+x)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{\\text{i}}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{\\text{j}}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{\\text{k}}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=yz{e}^{xz}+z,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{xz}+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{xz}+x\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (yz{e}^{xz}+z)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =y{e}^{xz}+xz+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{xz}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{xz}+1$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{xz}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & ={e}^{xz}+1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =y+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=y+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xz}+xz+y+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{xz}+x+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{xz}+x$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy{e}^{xz}+x+{h}^{′}(z) & =zy{e}^{xz}+x \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xz}+xz+y+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406696 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dd49044-48d7-5753-8938-92019f630b52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+2y{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406667} {:answer/id #uuid "4d50a1c5-e1f1-531f-8432-aafd884d17cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+2yz+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406672} {:answer/id #uuid "7f2af6d4-f404-59ca-99d2-24985eb2eafa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{3}z+y{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406678} {:answer/id #uuid "a809662b-6dd9-5c73-b6ef-ca6fafbec01c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}yz+y+z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406681} {:answer/id #uuid "b668a6c8-35b7-56c2-aa49-6197e1a607d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+yz+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f2af6d4-f404-59ca-99d2-24985eb2eafa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{3}z+y{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406678} :answer-field/id #uuid "419ffafb-e705-5c7d-80bf-60c8356135f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406691}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "327918f1-3cba-54fe-8e7b-c743d7b1d3cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-81755" :question/problem "Consider the function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=2x{y}^{3}z\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+{z}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+({x}^{2}{y}^{3}+2yz)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{i}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,\\text{j}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,\\text{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x{y}^{3}z,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+{z}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={x}^{2}{y}^{3}+2yz\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 2x{y}^{3}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{y}^{3}z+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+{z}^{2}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & ={z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int {z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =y{z}^{2}+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=y{z}^{2}+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{3}z+y{z}^{2}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={x}^{2}{y}^{3}+2yz+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={x}^{2}{y}^{3}+2yz$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}+2yz+{h}^{′}(z) & ={x}^{2}{y}^{3}+2yz \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{3}z+y{z}^{2}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406698 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58749cbe-7816-57fd-a7c2-054a48490984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2x{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406675} {:answer/id #uuid "5d64b8a8-da33-5a82-92ab-d47162348e5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=xy-{y}^{2}+2yz+{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406676} {:answer/id #uuid "b90e506d-36bb-59dc-a9d8-181dd55c4171" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+z{y}^{2}-y{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406685} {:answer/id #uuid "c3d21bb7-6a0c-5042-8d17-4fbbdd6ece2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}y-xy+x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406687} {:answer/id #uuid "ea19559e-ae30-58d1-a09e-446a3ce435cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+xy+{y}^{2}+yz-{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea19559e-ae30-58d1-a09e-446a3ce435cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+xy+{y}^{2}+yz-{z}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406689} :answer-field/id #uuid "a46e9509-621a-57db-9c8d-caf61cc840c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406693}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a894d767-b55b-50b3-ac91-79c05f30a84d" :question/math-academy-id "q-124731" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=(2x+y)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(2y+x+z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+(y-2z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,k.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x+y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y+x+z,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=y-2z\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2x+y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+xy+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y+x+z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =2y+x+z \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =2y+z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int (2y+z)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={y}^{2}+yz+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)={y}^{2}+yz+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+xy+{y}^{2}+yz+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=y+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=y-2z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-2z & =y+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =-2z \\\\ h(z) & =-{z}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+xy+{y}^{2}+yz-{z}^{2}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498537 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34800481-715e-5257-9d4c-7d037cac6fef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=4{x}^{2}y+yz+z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497915} {:answer/id #uuid "9cf158fb-4d25-5864-9cb6-eb9d3f393756" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2{x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}z+z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498152} {:answer/id #uuid "cd789499-1240-527d-ba30-e55b7342f064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+yz+xz+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498261} {:answer/id #uuid "cdace420-7534-506a-9578-b4e2449a1989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2{x}^{2}z+{y}^{2}z+y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498262} {:answer/id #uuid "f9ae4394-1680-5b98-a6cf-4a436850cd18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2}+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cf158fb-4d25-5864-9cb6-eb9d3f393756" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2{x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}z+z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498152} :answer-field/id #uuid "2575d212-1190-514e-a919-fd516555543d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498374}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "556e4e71-69c2-58ca-8978-843d74c13525" :question/math-academy-id "q-132102" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y,z)=\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z),$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=4xy\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(2{x}^{2}+2yz)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+({y}^{2}+1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,k.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=4xy,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}+2yz,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={y}^{2}+1\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 4xy\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}y+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}+2yz$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =2{x}^{2}+2yz \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =2yz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 2yz\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={y}^{2}z+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)={y}^{2}z+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=2{x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}z+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={y}^{2}+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={y}^{2}+1$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+1 & ={y}^{2}+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =1 \\\\ h(z) & =z+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=2{x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}z+z+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567647 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "192fa087-d083-5924-ae98-cd7d625ab4af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=3 y z + 2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567648} {:answer/id #uuid "5b3a1d82-130c-5da3-89ee-0a8fcc4d3a3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=6 y z + 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567655} {:answer/id #uuid "76d73b62-4a86-5d81-a70b-31c9ec1badea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=3 y z^{2} + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567657} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe24e83-8f50-5d0a-b75d-1e2dc303d3ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=3 y^{2} z + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567673} {:answer/id #uuid "edbe968b-0c7e-5691-8506-64ade75652a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=6 y^{2} z + 2 \\sin^{2}{\\left(2 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfe24e83-8f50-5d0a-b75d-1e2dc303d3ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=3 y^{2} z + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567673} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d2330e0-c551-5af7-9f6c-bffd77f8e497" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567656}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "17f552c9-999e-5c31-bcd5-7f533396345c" :question/problem "Consider the function\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,z)&=\\left(4 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{}+\\left(6 y z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &{}+\\left(3 y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=4 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=6 y z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=3 y^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(4 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=6 y z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=6 y z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=\\int \\left(6 y z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=3 y^{2} z+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=3 y^{2} z+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=3 y^{2} z + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=3 y^{2}+h'(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=3 y^{2}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 y^{2}+h'(z)&=3 y^{2} \\\\ h'(z)&=0 \\\\ h(z)&=C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=3 y^{2} z + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567650 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09ba08eb-e249-5d3e-bca5-2ff400729dc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=e^{x y} + \\cos{\\left(2 z \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567644} {:answer/id #uuid "11fc51a6-42c2-5913-8ae0-b274472c5530" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=e^{x y} + \\sin{\\left(2 z \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567645} {:answer/id #uuid "b894fd2b-6b06-5050-a041-0ca7bf9e397d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x e^{x y} + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 z \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567667} {:answer/id #uuid "b9813030-8e9f-5a03-a282-00dc575f4177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=y e^{x y} + 2 \\cos{\\left(2 z \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567668} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5e91fc-9a3e-5c7b-acf5-4eac32ec196b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x e^{x y} + y e^{x y} + \\cos{\\left(2 z \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11fc51a6-42c2-5913-8ae0-b274472c5530" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=e^{x y} + \\sin{\\left(2 z \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567645} :answer-field/id #uuid "a659eb67-dff8-5f77-84af-73dbd8518337" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567664}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3ba1d91d-3adb-5f06-8cce-531d6cf8886c" :question/problem "Consider the function\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,z)&=\\left(y e^{x y}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{}+\\left(x e^{x y}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &{}+\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(2 z \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=y e^{x y} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=x e^{x y} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=2 \\cos{\\left(2 z \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(y e^{x y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=e^{x y}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=x e^{x y}+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=x e^{x y}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x e^{x y}+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=x e^{x y} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=\\int \\left(0\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=e^{x y}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=h'(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=2 \\cos{\\left(2 z \\right)}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h'(z)&=2 \\cos{\\left(2 z \\right)} \\\\ h(z)&=\\sin{\\left(2 z \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=e^{x y} + \\sin{\\left(2 z \\right)}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567663 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5854171c-e151-5f6a-a895-0cdc8fbf1d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- x e^{z} + 3 y^{3} z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567654} {:answer/id #uuid "7897149b-f106-5ecb-af76-ab3809bebeaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=3 x y z - y e^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567658} {:answer/id #uuid "ac2f5db4-4e9f-57aa-8a8f-63fe49a21655" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=3 x y^{2} z^{3} - x e^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567665} {:answer/id #uuid "bbdc1fb5-d533-52aa-8b9d-77e2d8f39bd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=3 x^{3} y^{2} + x z - e^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567669} {:answer/id #uuid "f674e8af-1419-5f9a-80d1-e728dd459f44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=3 x y^{2} z^{3} + y z - e^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac2f5db4-4e9f-57aa-8a8f-63fe49a21655" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=3 x y^{2} z^{3} - x e^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567665} :answer-field/id #uuid "a25c46a0-37f0-54b1-a8d4-b0289ca46f8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567662}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a64855d2-b9cc-5f61-84ab-7b355ca0ccfc" :question/problem "Consider the function\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,z)&=\\left(3 y^{2} z^{3} - e^{z}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{}+\\left(6 x y z^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &{}+\\left(9 x y^{2} z^{2} - x e^{z}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=3 y^{2} z^{3} - e^{z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=6 x y z^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=9 x y^{2} z^{2} - x e^{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(3 y^{2} z^{3} - e^{z}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=3 x y^{2} z^{3} - x e^{z}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=6 x y z^{3}+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=6 x y z^{3}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 x y z^{3}+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=6 x y z^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=\\int \\left(0\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=3 x y^{2} z^{3} - x e^{z}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=9 x y^{2} z^{2} - x e^{z}+h'(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=9 x y^{2} z^{2} - x e^{z}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 x y^{2} z^{2} - x e^{z}+h'(z)&=9 x y^{2} z^{2} - x e^{z} \\\\ h'(z)&=0 \\\\ h(z)&=C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=3 x y^{2} z^{3} - x e^{z}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dfa7364-65e6-50e7-97d1-b307b8add239" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y z - 2 x + 3 y + 3 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567653} {:answer/id #uuid "a1dc33a1-a52a-5b65-b13c-63a350a0979d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y - 2 x + 3 y z + 3 y + 3 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567661} {:answer/id #uuid "c145ac1d-eca6-5652-8103-7dfc4940e7fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y z - 2 x y - 2 x z + 3 y z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567670} {:answer/id #uuid "df30551a-5afc-52d4-b506-21ef92075c90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y - 2 x z + 3 y z + 3 y + 3 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567674} {:answer/id #uuid "fba3a637-071a-5bca-a98b-43913edce123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y + 3 x z - 2 x + 3 y z + 3 y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1dc33a1-a52a-5b65-b13c-63a350a0979d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y - 2 x + 3 y z + 3 y + 3 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567661} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e918e7d-104e-52fe-8744-d26aeff22795" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567651}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b76a0ba0-27a6-50a6-b5a4-4084dcfb3438" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,z)&=\\left(- 2 y - 2\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{}+\\left(- 2 x + 3 z + 3\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &{}+\\left(3 y + 3\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=- 2 y - 2 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- 2 x + 3 z + 3 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=3 y + 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(- 2 y - 2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=- 2 x y - 2 x+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=- 2 x+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=- 2 x + 3 z + 3$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 2 x+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=- 2 x + 3 z + 3 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=3 z + 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=\\int \\left(3 z + 3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=3 y z + 3 y+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=3 y z + 3 y+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=- 2 x y - 2 x + 3 y z + 3 y+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=3 y+h'(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=3 y + 3$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 y+h'(z)&=3 y + 3 \\\\ h'(z)&=3 \\\\ h(z)&=3 z+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=- 2 x y - 2 x + 3 y z + 3 y + 3 z+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567671 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17db3bb9-e64e-55fc-86f9-5ae5c82de9d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x^{3} y^{2} + 2 x z - 2 e^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567646} {:answer/id #uuid "2b297faa-1274-51cf-b240-f912ee0ff779" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y^{2} z^{3} - 2 x e^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567649} {:answer/id #uuid "4b24e07e-5eff-5b2f-8b1f-ce8ca3c82270" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x e^{z} + 2 y^{3} z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567652} {:answer/id #uuid "92b1b649-39fe-5e83-838d-eb47b98ac13f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y^{2} z^{3} + 2 y z - 2 e^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567659} {:answer/id #uuid "f9bab808-77e4-5cfd-900f-674295ea2e2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y z - 2 y e^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b297faa-1274-51cf-b240-f912ee0ff779" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y^{2} z^{3} - 2 x e^{z}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567649} :answer-field/id #uuid "95b237dd-9011-5b59-97b6-c1d14da8d4d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567660}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c720b6f7-16fa-539b-bc2c-a22172819518" :question/problem "Consider the function\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,z)&=\\left(2 y^{2} z^{3} - 2 e^{z}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{}+\\left(4 x y z^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &{}+\\left(6 x y^{2} z^{2} - 2 x e^{z}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=2 y^{2} z^{3} - 2 e^{z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=4 x y z^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=6 x y^{2} z^{2} - 2 x e^{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(2 y^{2} z^{3} - 2 e^{z}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=2 x y^{2} z^{3} - 2 x e^{z}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=4 x y z^{3}+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=4 x y z^{3}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 x y z^{3}+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=4 x y z^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=\\int \\left(0\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=2 x y^{2} z^{3} - 2 x e^{z}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=6 x y^{2} z^{2} - 2 x e^{z}+h'(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=6 x y^{2} z^{2} - 2 x e^{z}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 x y^{2} z^{2} - 2 x e^{z}+h'(z)&=6 x y^{2} z^{2} - 2 x e^{z} \\\\ h'(z)&=0 \\\\ h(z)&=C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=2 x y^{2} z^{3} - 2 x e^{z}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712546 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "156ab6d0-b3b1-5b04-bf1f-0facbf9e8e26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + x^{2} y + y^{2} z + z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712544} {:answer/id #uuid "451661a8-9e18-539a-91e9-819b3f17aecf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + x^{2} y + 2 y^{2} z - z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712547} {:answer/id #uuid "7404ad64-3a02-5a76-8965-b493c299cd42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + x^{2} y + y^{2} z + y - z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712549} {:answer/id #uuid "dd1d5c46-76c1-54ca-9b36-00596dd96f62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + x^{2} y + y^{2} z - z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712559} {:answer/id #uuid "f4265c27-7a37-53cf-aae6-66003b3da45c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + x^{2} y + y^{2} z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd1d5c46-76c1-54ca-9b36-00596dd96f62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + x^{2} y + y^{2} z - z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712559} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff855a93-8c45-528f-81d1-3e56161ad607" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712564}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2878b7ac-d720-5bcb-afc7-375c8c621401" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that\n\n$$\n\\nabla f=\\mathbf F=2xy\\,\\mathbf i+(x^2+2yz)\\,\\mathbf j+(y^2-2z)\\,\\mathbf k.\n$$\n\nSelect the family of functions whose gradient is $\\mathbf F$. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "The components of the gradient give\n\n$$\nf_x=2xy,\\qquad f_y=x^2+2yz,\\qquad f_z=y^2-2z.\n$$\n\nIntegrate the first equation with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x^2y+g(y,z).\n$$\n\nThe integration term is a function of $y$ and $z$, since every term independent of $x$ vanishes when differentiated with respect to $x$. Differentiate with respect to $y$ and match the second component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^2+g_y(y,z)&=x^2+2yz,\\\\\ng_y(y,z)&=2yz,\\\\\ng(y,z)&=y^2z+h(z).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $f=x^2y+y^2z+h(z)$. The third component determines the remaining function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_z&=y^2+h'(z),\\\\\ny^2+h'(z)&=y^2-2z,\\\\\nh'(z)&=-2z,\\\\\nh(z)&=-z^2+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x^2y+y^2z-z^2+C.\n$$\n\nChecking all components gives $f_x=2xy$, $f_y=x^2+2yz$, and $f_z=y^2-2z$. Stopping after the first integration would miss the terms needed by the other two components."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712554 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48bcc1a9-fec6-5c51-9752-20f7ff4a7d89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + x^{2} y + y z + 2 z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712548} {:answer/id #uuid "8e2da164-d0b7-5db1-b0e3-a9136e389fa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + x^{2} y + y z + z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712552} {:answer/id #uuid "ceb68cf3-0a59-5a80-b4c2-1636d805ea45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + x^{2} y + y z - z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712555} {:answer/id #uuid "f068bca5-4363-5a77-88b0-0731776ea71e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + x^{2} y + y z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712561} {:answer/id #uuid "f1341e46-a14b-50cf-9dc4-b422062b1556" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + x^{2} y + y z + 2 z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e2da164-d0b7-5db1-b0e3-a9136e389fa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + x^{2} y + y z + z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712552} :answer-field/id #uuid "d88d2fea-d028-54a9-9087-38aa974c3f67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712557}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a9d2624d-2d23-51c3-9f63-063380a1bd6d" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that\n\n$$\n\\nabla f=\\mathbf F=2xy\\,\\mathbf i+(x^2+z)\\,\\mathbf j+(y+2z)\\,\\mathbf k.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the first component with respect to $x$ and matching the second component has already given\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x^2y+yz+h(z).\n$$\n\nUse the third component to determine $h(z)$ and select the resulting family of functions. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "The components of $\\mathbf F$ require $f_x=2xy$, $f_y=x^2+z$, and $f_z=y+2z$. The supplied expression already satisfies the first two equations: differentiating $x^2y+yz+h(z)$ gives $f_x=2xy$ and $f_y=x^2+z$.\n\nDifferentiate it with respect to $z$ and compare with the third component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_z&=y+h'(z),\\\\\ny+h'(z)&=y+2z,\\\\\nh'(z)&=2z.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\nh(z)=\\int 2z\\,\\mathrm dz=z^2+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitution gives\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x^2y+yz+z^2+C.\n$$\n\nIts three partial derivatives are $2xy$, $x^2+z$, and $y+2z$, as required. An additive constant has zero gradient."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712560 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c22a77c-90a9-512b-9e67-a2be5fa7393e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + y z + y e^{x z} - z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712545} {:answer/id #uuid "81bdeccd-8db3-5500-83ff-bbc6d8fbb5f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + y z + y e^{x z} + z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712551} {:answer/id #uuid "9d5b3af3-5d6c-5e19-a26a-f2e9ed02ce36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + y z + y e^{x z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712553} {:answer/id #uuid "d77d4662-5a1e-5c82-abfa-40f3069a9632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + y^{2} + y z + y e^{x z} - z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712556} {:answer/id #uuid "d99c4ceb-87a0-55a3-9d73-b6ad749a5796" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + y z + y e^{x z} - z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d99c4ceb-87a0-55a3-9d73-b6ad749a5796" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=C + y z + y e^{x z} - z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712558} :answer-field/id #uuid "795db9ad-6ec6-5dce-aaaf-a62e8d9195d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712550}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ecef7eaa-7399-5ee5-b312-4d95eeb05ee2" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that\n\n$$\n\\nabla f=\\mathbf F=yz e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf i+(e^{xz}+z)\\,\\mathbf j+(xy e^{xz}+y-2z)\\,\\mathbf k.\n$$\n\nSelect the family of functions whose gradient is $\\mathbf F$. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "We need\n\n$$\nf_x=yz e^{xz},\\qquad f_y=e^{xz}+z,\\qquad f_z=xy e^{xz}+y-2z.\n$$\n\nFor the first integration, $y$ and $z$ are held constant. Since $\\partial(e^{xz})/\\partial x=z e^{xz}$, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=y e^{xz}+g(y,z).\n$$\n\nThis antiderivative is valid also at $z=0$; no division by $z$ is needed. Differentiating with respect to $y$ and matching the second component gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ne^{xz}+g_y(y,z)&=e^{xz}+z,\\\\\ng_y(y,z)&=z,\\\\\ng(y,z)&=yz+h(z).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow $f=y e^{xz}+yz+h(z)$. When differentiating with respect to $z$, the exponential contributes a factor of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_z&=xy e^{xz}+y+h'(z),\\\\\nxy e^{xz}+y+h'(z)&=xy e^{xz}+y-2z,\\\\\nh'(z)&=-2z,\\\\\nh(z)&=-z^2+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=y e^{xz}+yz-z^2+C.\n$$\n\nThe check is $f_x=yz e^{xz}$, $f_y=e^{xz}+z$, and $f_z=xy e^{xz}+y-2z$. All three components agree; the first component alone cannot determine the terms independent of $x$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "766b3bf2-3cf4-5c1d-82a5-46e731d7ff41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y + 2 y z + 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712928} {:answer/id #uuid "db0d3bd4-9300-5382-b0dd-622292bcf26d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y - y z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712937} {:answer/id #uuid "ee76916a-5b44-5569-9645-57de3335fd0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y - 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712940} {:answer/id #uuid "ef4d1b44-30d8-560d-9514-d205cc9c2da8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y + y z + z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712941} {:answer/id #uuid "f2fb92ce-7114-5063-b5dd-502ea56d9bb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y - 2 y z - z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee76916a-5b44-5569-9645-57de3335fd0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y - 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712940} :answer-field/id #uuid "a86a318f-06e5-54f4-acfd-f308b10fa615" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712934}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1016dc15-7408-5b3c-94f3-88a8e6a6fd18" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,z)&=\\left(- 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{}+\\left(- 2 x\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &{}+\\left(-2\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=- 2 y \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- 2 x \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(- 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=- 2 x y+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=- 2 x+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=- 2 x$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 2 x+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=- 2 x \\\\ \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=\\int \\left(0\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=- 2 x y+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=h'(z).\n$$\n\nComparing this derivative with the third component and subtracting the known terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h'(z)&=-2 \\\\ h(z)&=- 2 z+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=- 2 x y - 2 z+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712919 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15ae8d87-a954-5572-8703-7d7b0c3dac08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x y - y z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712916} {:answer/id #uuid "63c2eed4-5c7a-5679-9bd2-7a7e87244f2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x y + 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712926} {:answer/id #uuid "87d0d58b-d73c-504a-b43c-098aba258ec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x y + y z - z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712929} {:answer/id #uuid "f595bbd9-b32d-5ea5-acd6-a666812a905e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x y + 2 y z + z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712945} {:answer/id #uuid "fdd4d5fc-3f06-51cb-be3b-9a3e31e78dc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x y - 2 y z - 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87d0d58b-d73c-504a-b43c-098aba258ec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=x y + y z - z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712929} :answer-field/id #uuid "5471bc53-e8c7-5507-abc1-46fd15b8b84d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712922}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3721304e-cc24-5967-8502-ec2a900d9833" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,z)&=\\left(y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{}+\\left(x + z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &{}+\\left(y - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=y \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=x + z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=y - 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=x y+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=x+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=x + z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=x + z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=\\int \\left(z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=y z+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=y z+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x y + y z+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=y+h'(z).\n$$\n\nComparing this derivative with the third component and subtracting the known terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h'(z)&=-1 \\\\ h(z)&=- z+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x y + y z - z+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712936 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "377e3e7d-e882-572a-8aaa-e9e93339468b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y + 2 y z + 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712920} {:answer/id #uuid "5b573c53-652c-5eba-9b2e-bf876560b51d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y - y z + z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712924} {:answer/id #uuid "7154bf6f-58b9-587b-a0f0-66f8ac25b591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y - z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712927} {:answer/id #uuid "f3d74770-35af-5ed5-afd5-5832db04ff5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y + y z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712944} {:answer/id #uuid "f9d1d193-a935-5613-a0a5-c2aec2695ebc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y - 2 y z - 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "377e3e7d-e882-572a-8aaa-e9e93339468b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y + 2 y z + 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712920} :answer-field/id #uuid "152b8092-13b6-5fcf-8b50-b6b7c36cb33c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712915}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b392a4c7-1613-55a4-9bb0-7df5b6ac44ee" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,z)&=\\left(2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{}+\\left(2 x + 2 z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &{}+\\left(2 y + 2\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=2 y \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=2 x + 2 z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=2 y + 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(2 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=2 x y+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=2 x+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=2 x + 2 z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 x+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=2 x + 2 z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=2 z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=\\int \\left(2 z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=2 y z+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=2 y z+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=2 x y + 2 y z+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=2 y+h'(z).\n$$\n\nComparing this derivative with the third component and subtracting the known terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h'(z)&=2 \\\\ h(z)&=2 z+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=2 x y + 2 y z + 2 z+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712938 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04402fa1-b049-5767-9bbf-09346d98db14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- x y + y z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712913} {:answer/id #uuid "256ca264-1100-5ca9-a392-94a093184564" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- x y + 2 y z + 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712917} {:answer/id #uuid "5e5e9968-7d01-5417-adcf-bb5511b44679" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- x y - 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712925} {:answer/id #uuid "8d5212e8-d7b7-5d86-9c05-f66459fc4b45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- x y - y z + z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712930} {:answer/id #uuid "a2b03cd0-b4a2-5eb7-840f-4c5576427bd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- x y - 2 y z - z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d5212e8-d7b7-5d86-9c05-f66459fc4b45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- x y - y z + z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712930} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ec9f1d6-f987-5af3-84c4-1edfb99a5953" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712932}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dd1ffc50-f49f-52e2-8188-d34fa23d8198" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,z)&=\\left(- y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{}+\\left(- x - z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &{}+\\left(1 - y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=- y \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- x - z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=1 - y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(- y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=- x y+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=- x+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=- x - z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- x+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=- x - z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=- z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=\\int \\left(- z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=- y z+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=- y z+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=- x y - y z+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=- y+h'(z).\n$$\n\nComparing this derivative with the third component and subtracting the known terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h'(z)&=1 \\\\ h(z)&=z+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=- x y - y z + z+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712942 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "305018ed-59e7-5b60-9e07-a470c52ec409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 3 x y + 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712918} {:answer/id #uuid "3cfbf66c-46ce-5b5c-bc3d-833d087922bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 3 x y - y z - 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712921} {:answer/id #uuid "9192a2ec-76f1-5204-9d67-39acb9247368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 3 x y - 2 y z + z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712931} {:answer/id #uuid "b0e2f4e5-5a12-5f83-8aef-adc2142c0245" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 3 x y + y z - z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712935} {:answer/id #uuid "e9a7dfac-08b6-5c5d-a68f-e0b3a6832b3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 3 x y + 2 y z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9192a2ec-76f1-5204-9d67-39acb9247368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 3 x y - 2 y z + z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712931} :answer-field/id #uuid "59530361-6c8c-54b0-b382-5810791deed5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712923}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0deb6f6-d948-59cb-bc83-2db33e36198b" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,z)&=\\left(- 3 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{}+\\left(- 3 x - 2 z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &{}+\\left(1 - 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=- 3 y \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- 3 x - 2 z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=1 - 2 y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(- 3 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=- 3 x y+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=- 3 x+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=- 3 x - 2 z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 3 x+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=- 3 x - 2 z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=- 2 z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=\\int \\left(- 2 z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=- 2 y z+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=- 2 y z+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=- 3 x y - 2 y z+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=- 2 y+h'(z).\n$$\n\nComparing this derivative with the third component and subtracting the known terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h'(z)&=1 \\\\ h(z)&=z+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=- 3 x y - 2 y z + z+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712980 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11b7ab67-87f6-57e7-8bbf-96a519ad6aa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 3 x y - 3 x + 4 y z + 4 y + 4 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712979} {:answer/id #uuid "3b6a620d-b03b-5e96-874d-3f03699cd5f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 3 x y - 3 x - 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712983} {:answer/id #uuid "772fcd05-4c47-5c7f-bf08-d168c4a6e85c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 3 x y - 3 x - 4 y z - 4 y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712989} {:answer/id #uuid "c270ef30-8b05-5d63-8b89-6cc1740a7c09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 3 x y - 3 x - 2 y z - 2 y - 4 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712998} {:answer/id #uuid "c6c3646c-6468-59e1-8daa-99bee56ee817" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 3 x y - 3 x + 2 y z + 2 y + 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b6a620d-b03b-5e96-874d-3f03699cd5f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 3 x y - 3 x - 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712983} :answer-field/id #uuid "b535389e-dd31-5fbe-910f-1b8b32e248cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712996}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c7135ae-c94d-5387-96b7-89f9fda0c335" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,z)&=\\left(- 3 y - 3\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{}+\\left(- 3 x\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &{}+\\left(-2\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=- 3 y - 3 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- 3 x \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(- 3 y - 3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=- 3 x y - 3 x+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=- 3 x+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=- 3 x$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 3 x+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=- 3 x \\\\ \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=\\int \\left(0\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=- 3 x y - 3 x+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=h'(z).\n$$\n\nComparing this derivative with the third component and subtracting the known terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h'(z)&=-2 \\\\ h(z)&=- 2 z+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=- 3 x y - 3 x - 2 z+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712981 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39c40759-853c-560e-96d7-6c6b41fab0a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y z^{2} - 6 y z - 12 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712982} {:answer/id #uuid "d28906c0-59a1-565f-a21d-fb6d7346d5e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y z^{2} - 6 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713000} {:answer/id #uuid "dd3e55bb-0644-5c25-9a25-e68157ee2038" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y z^{2} + 6 y z + 12 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713001} {:answer/id #uuid "e7728367-6c53-57c3-8e30-3d8609fd4db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y z^{2} + 3 y z + 6 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713002} {:answer/id #uuid "fe2e0124-24a6-5b1e-859b-66599e5ffee6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y z^{2} - 3 y z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39c40759-853c-560e-96d7-6c6b41fab0a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y z^{2} - 6 y z - 12 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712982} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ab44dd7-193a-5569-9c04-fabf403c6777" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712991}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25ba31f9-0121-556b-a6a5-2aeafff61b3e" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,z)&=\\left(- 2 y z^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{}+\\left(- 2 x z^{2} - 6 z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &{}+\\left(- 4 x y z - 6 y - 12\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=- 2 y z^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- 2 x z^{2} - 6 z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=- 4 x y z - 6 y - 12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(- 2 y z^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=- 2 x y z^{2}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=- 2 x z^{2}+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=- 2 x z^{2} - 6 z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 2 x z^{2}+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=- 2 x z^{2} - 6 z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=- 6 z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=\\int \\left(- 6 z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=- 6 y z+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=- 6 y z+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=- 2 x y z^{2} - 6 y z+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=- 4 x y z - 6 y+h'(z).\n$$\n\nComparing this derivative with the third component and subtracting the known terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h'(z)&=-12 \\\\ h(z)&=- 12 z+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=- 2 x y z^{2} - 6 y z - 12 z+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d9d765e-ac11-5c04-8d2f-72a95754718f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x^{2} y - 4 y^{2} z - 4 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712977} {:answer/id #uuid "4df92987-d6e4-58c3-9e76-a4c193f86b4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x^{2} y + 4 y^{2} z - 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712986} {:answer/id #uuid "58b773b9-36eb-5cdc-ab84-7ac8844f949c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x^{2} y + 2 y^{2} z + 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712987} {:answer/id #uuid "b5554ce2-5792-55fe-922c-bc9b106203e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x^{2} y - 2 y^{2} z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712997} {:answer/id #uuid "f22ffeeb-bfa1-5ba1-bd6e-a2233dd16a00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x^{2} y + 4 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d9d765e-ac11-5c04-8d2f-72a95754718f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x^{2} y - 4 y^{2} z - 4 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712977} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bdbab53-3835-5fa0-88fe-42d6dfbdd3c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712985}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "856251cb-b05a-5070-8c59-6c1c47e57d6b" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,z)&=\\left(4 x y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{}+\\left(2 x^{2} - 8 y z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &{}+\\left(- 4 y^{2} - 4\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=4 x y \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=2 x^{2} - 8 y z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=- 4 y^{2} - 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(4 x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=2 x^{2} y+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=2 x^{2}+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=2 x^{2} - 8 y z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 x^{2}+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=2 x^{2} - 8 y z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=- 8 y z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=\\int \\left(- 8 y z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=- 4 y^{2} z+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=- 4 y^{2} z+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=2 x^{2} y - 4 y^{2} z+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=- 4 y^{2}+h'(z).\n$$\n\nComparing this derivative with the third component and subtracting the known terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h'(z)&=-4 \\\\ h(z)&=- 4 z+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=2 x^{2} y - 4 y^{2} z - 4 z+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712995 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "413d2aec-275b-5493-b9a1-846ba3804f29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y z^{2} - 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712984} {:answer/id #uuid "623caa14-9211-5f08-a097-63f7644bddf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y z^{2} + y z + 4 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712988} {:answer/id #uuid "8c535718-2c3b-55a5-89d2-43ac67bc4db4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y z^{2} + 2 y z - 4 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712992} {:answer/id #uuid "95ecd286-b13a-5338-b5e1-07763aee942e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y z^{2} - 2 y z + 2 z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712993} {:answer/id #uuid "9b3640d8-3c30-57a4-a54c-ea3ebe4dc55b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y z^{2} - y z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b3640d8-3c30-57a4-a54c-ea3ebe4dc55b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x,y,z)=2 x y z^{2} - y z+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712994} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fc35b65-bb4a-509f-9577-6457f28f96ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712978}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ad464312-69a5-5333-b56e-2b85d95a8534" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,z)&=\\left(2 y z^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{}+\\left(2 x z^{2} - z\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &{}+\\left(4 x y z - y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,\\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\nabla f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=2 y z^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=2 x z^{2} - z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=4 x y z - y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\int \\left(2 y z^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=2 x y z^{2}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=2 x z^{2}+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}=2 x z^{2} - z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 x z^{2}+\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=2 x z^{2} - z \\\\ \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}&=- z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z)&=\\int \\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=\\int \\left(- z\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &=- y z+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=- y z+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=2 x y z^{2} - y z+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}=4 x y z - y+h'(z).\n$$\n\nComparing this derivative with the third component and subtracting the known terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h'(z)&=0 \\\\ h(z)&=C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=2 x y z^{2} - y z+C.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Reconstructing a Three-Variable Function From Its Gradient"}]}
